# ============================================================================
# ROUTE 29, expanded  (44x14 blocks, buffer 1000/1300; vanilla 30x9)
# Source: route29_base.amap (hand grid); this file = rough.py --seed 3 --p 0.55
# ============================================================================
# KEPT: W->E route, Cherrygrove W, New Bark E; Route 46 gate at the top
#   middle; first tall grass right at the New Bark end and ON the road so
#   the first wild battle happens here; one-way ledges; headbutt trees;
#   fruit tree; the same NPC cast (Fisher, Cooltrainers, Youngster, Teacher,
#   Tuscany on Tuesdays) and the Potion.
# ADDED (cf. pokefollow Route 1 10x18 -> 19x24, which got a river/cliff band):
#   Upper tier: a raised meadow north of a long ledge, reached only by the
#     gate path. West half = fruit grove; east half = a woodland pond with
#     the Fisher (Old Rod tease) and the Potion on the far bank.
#   Rest cabin (2c-2f) south of the gate: the no-Center waypoint (rest +
#     watch, PC box). Doubles as Route 29's landmark building.
#   Stands of wood that break the route into rooms; ragged forest edges.
#   South meadows of tall grass below a second ledge: optional trainers,
#     Tuscany, items; three loops back to the road.
# CONNECTIONS: W row 6 (steps 12-13), E row 8-9 (steps 16-19), N gate door
#   at (41,1). Gate top half lives in Route 46's connection strip as vanilla.
# ============================================================================
ref Route29
key x=1a y=11 1=2c 2=2d 3=2e 4=2f Q=03
key !=3c ?=3d @=3e $=3f &=64 +=62 |=60 <=5d >=5e %=61 /=5c
